{
  "$about": [
    "Index of every project's images, for fast lookup when asked to replace one.",
    "This is a reference file only -- nothing on the live site reads it. The site",
    "is static .dc.html with no component framework and no build step, so the",
    "actual source of truth stays where it already lived: Moe Ali Portfolio.dc.html",
    "(homepage cards) and Project.dc.html's Component.DATA object (case-study copy).",
    "This file exists so those two places don't have to be re-read from scratch",
    "every time -- it is kept in sync by hand whenever an image or copy changes."
  ],
  "$imageMechanics": [
    "Every image is an <image-slot id=\"...\"> custom element, not a plain <img>.",
    "Two ways a slot gets a picture, in priority order:",
    "  1. .image-slots.state.json[slotId].u -- a dropped-in image (base64), set",
    "     via the Claude Design canvas UI. This WINS if present, silently, even",
    "     if the tag also has a src= attribute.",
    "  2. The slot tag's own src=\"uploads/...\" attribute -- the fallback used",
    "     when no sidecar entry exists. This is what a manual file edit controls.",
    "So: before editing a src= attribute and wondering why nothing changed,",
    "check whether .image-slots.state.json already has an entry for that slot id.",
    "Cover slot ids (work-1..work-6) are SHARED between the homepage grid card",
    "and that project's case-study hero -- filling one fills both automatically.",
    "Gallery slots (cs-<slug>-2..8) exist ONLY inside Project.dc.html's template",
    "as {{ slot2 }}..{{ slot8 }} -- they have no src= attribute in the markup at",
    "all, so they can only ever be filled via the sidecar, never by editing HTML.",
    "Wide/square pairs (work-3/work-3-sq, work-6/work-6-sq) both need filling --",
    "the square crop is what actually shows below 860px viewport width."
  ],
